Since you have already set this up on your laptop, the command you are looking for is:

```bash
clasp push
```

### Here are the common commands you might need:

1.  **`clasp push`**: This is the primary command. It uploads all your local files (like `Code.js`) to the Google Apps Script server. If you have a `.claspignore` file, it will respect those rules.
2.  **`clasp push -w`**: This is the "watch" mode. It will stay active and automatically push your changes every time you save a file locally.
3.  **`clasp login`**: If your session has expired or you get an authorization error, run this to re-authenticate with your Google account.
4.  **`clasp status`**: If you want to see which files will be pushed or ignored before you run the command.

### Quick Tip for your `JABA` project:
Make sure you are in the `/home/rey_miller_chancahuana_almora/JABA/` directory in your terminal before running the command so that `clasp` can find your `.clasp.json` configuration file.

